                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Pros:\n\nSimple concepts that anyone could grasp. Just avoid the yellow balls and try to collect some power ups. They introduce a new power up every level.\n\nThe games do not take very long so you could play them with only a few minutes of time.\n\nThe music is actually very good. It feels like the music is better than the game.\n\nCons:\n\nThe game is way to simple and I could find a game like it on a flash games site. \n\nMost of the powerups are not beneficial to pick up. The sheild and sometimes the shoting ones are the only ones ever worth getting. The bomb automaticly causes you to lose all of your star power, which isn't worth clearing the screen of everything, not just the yellow orbs. The time slowdown just causes the balls to stay on the screen longer, which can make things very compact. I find myself trying to avoid most the power ups than collect them\n\nThe music doesn't fit the game. This sounds like it contradicts the pro, but the music is way to detailed and good for such a simple game. It doesn't feel like it should be on this game at all and should be in a game with a little bit more detail.\n\nMost importantly, I did not find this game fun. Some people might, but it is not my cup of tea.",
